+// The mark of a Space with an Independent session (sessions S32-S34, spaces
+// B38; BACKLOG S-164). The session had shown only as a checked row in the
+// Space menu: nothing on screen told a Space with its own cookies from one
+// that shares the profile's, and pinning one of its tabs moved it into the
+// shared session without a word. Every surface that shows a Space now marks
+// it -- the switcher's chips in the open sidebar and in the rail, the name
+// floating over a chip, the title row in both forms, the command bar's rows,
+// the tab menu's Space rows, the routed toast, the archive page and
+// Settings -- and the mark goes from each when the session is turned off. A
+// pin out of such a Space says so, with an Undo. A Blank Window and a private
+// window have no jars and mark nothing.
